1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,840
Your phone keyboard guesses the next word.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,330
Look at the three suggestions above it.

3
00:00:05,515 --> 00:00:07,845
An LLM does the same thing,

4
00:00:08,095 --> 00:00:10,765
but with almost all the text
humans have ever written.

5
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:14,700
LLM stands for Large Language Model.

6
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:18,420
Large means billions of numbers inside it,
called parameters.

7
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,930
Language means it works with words.

8
00:00:21,295 --> 00:00:25,845
A model is just a pattern learner,
not a database and not a thinking brain.

9
00:00:26,983 --> 00:00:29,413
Say you type, the capital of India is.

10
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:31,383
The model answers New Delhi.

11
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,188
It does not open a page.

12
00:00:33,548 --> 00:00:35,478
It produces the answer from patterns

13
00:00:35,948 --> 00:00:37,578
it has seen millions of times.

14
00:00:37,908 --> 00:00:41,198
Ask about something rare,
and it still writes a smooth sentence.

15
00:00:42,383 --> 00:00:44,133
Training is simple to describe.

16
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:46,373
It reads a huge pile of text.

17
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:48,423
For every next word, it guesses,

18
00:00:48,973 --> 00:00:51,163
checks the answer, and nudges its numbers.

19
00:00:51,553 --> 00:00:53,343
A wrong guess is not a failure.

20
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:55,878
It is the signal that moves the numbers.

21
00:00:56,238 --> 00:00:58,008
Repeat that billions of times.

22
00:00:59,117 --> 00:01:00,227
The trick is attention.

23
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:01,937
When it reads a sentence,

24
00:01:02,307 --> 00:01:04,617
it weighs which words
matter for the next one.

25
00:01:04,847 --> 00:01:09,717
Like guessing the next line of a song from
the whole stanza, not just the last word.

26
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:13,997
That is why a word's meaning can
change with the sentence around it.

27
00:01:14,917 --> 00:01:17,467
At small scale, it is just autocomplete.

28
00:01:17,757 --> 00:01:21,607
At large scale, next word prediction
starts to look like reasoning.

29
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:26,852
The same machine can summarize a chapter,
translate a message, or write code.

30
00:01:27,162 --> 00:01:30,752
It can also follow instructions
and answer in your language.

31
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:33,000
But it is still guessing.

32
00:01:33,435 --> 00:01:36,965
It can be confidently wrong,
because it predicts plausible text,

33
00:01:37,075 --> 00:01:38,185
not checked facts.

34
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,970
Ask for a source, and it may invent one.

35
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:45,290
So verify anything important
with a book or a trusted website.

36
00:01:46,317 --> 00:01:49,927
An LLM is a very well
trained next word predictor.

37
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:51,927
Useful, but not magic.

